-- EXPERIMENT throughput-sweep query -- Sema translation of query/flockmtl/Q101.sql.
--
-- Sema expresses a semantic filter as a WHERE-clause string literal prefixed
-- with s, interpolating columns as {name}. The predicate text is kept
-- word-for-word identical to the flockmtl / LOTUS / Palimpzest arms ("The
-- following movie review is clearly positive.") so the only thing that differs
-- across arms is how the system drives the endpoint, not what it asks the model.
-- The one unavoidable addition is the ": {reviewText}" interpolation, because
-- Sema has no separate context_columns channel the way llm_filter does -- the
-- column goes inline in the predicate.
--
-- The flockmtl version aliases the table AS r and writes r.reviewText. The alias
-- is dropped here: it has no effect on the plan for a single-table scan, and a
-- bare {reviewText} is the form the Sema README documents.
--
-- No model-name placeholder: Sema takes its model from SET llm_model, which the
-- runner issues in the per-query SQL header, not from the query text. (Do not
-- write the jinja placeholder in these comments -- the runner renders the whole
-- file, so it would be substituted inside the comment too.)
SELECT reviewId
FROM reviews_2000
WHERE s'The following movie review is clearly positive: {reviewText}';
